# OpenSpec, TDD, and delivery gates

Canonical detail: [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md). OpenSpec config: [openspec/config.yaml](openspec/config.yaml).

## One spec, one branch

- Change name and Git branch: **`T-XX-YY-ZZ`**, derived from ticket **`T-XX-YY`** in [docs/7-tickets.md](docs/7-tickets.md).
- Multiple specs per ticket are normal; do not combine two ZZ values in one change or branch.

## SDD + TDD

- Create the OpenSpec change from the ticket (**Hace** / **Listo cuando**).
- Define tests (happy + **unhappy path**) in the change before or alongside implementation.
- Apply **Red → Green → Refactor**; DoD from [docs/6-historias.md](docs/6-historias.md) applies.
- **No git commits** during TDD on the spec branch; changes remain local until archive (see `git-agent-gates.mdc`).

## Archive and commit

- Run the agreed test suite; **all relevant tests must be green** before suggesting archive.
- Run `openspec validate` on the change when applicable.
- **`openspec archive`**: only when tests are green; execute only if the user explicitly authorizes (otherwise recommend the user run it).
- **Only after archive**: you may **propose** the **first** commit for that spec branch (Conventional Commits; see [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md) § 7). Never propose or run `git commit` before archive.
- Do **not** run `git commit` until the user authorizes (see `git-agent-gates.mdc`).

## Verification commands (when Rust workspace exists)

`cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace` — align with CI when [T-09-01](docs/7-tickets.md) exists.
